= Coordination problem — Simple =

A coordination problem happens when people or systems would benefit from making compatible choices, but they may fail because they do not know what the others will choose. Driving on the same side of the road is a classic example.

'''Important boundary:''' coordination problem ≠ collective-action problem by identity.

